"id": "B0",
"name": "hidden truth does not steer the Hound: with the prey silently somewhere else (hundreds of px away), the Hound does exactly the same, tick for tick, until it gets new evidence",
"ok": true,
"note": "10 paired runs; prey moved 703-1495 px between the worlds; identical for 1.39 s on average (0.95, 1.88, 0.02, 5.02, 0.95, 0.97, 0.95, 0.97, 1.43, 0.73), ended by new evidence / time; diverged without new evidence: 0"
},
{
"id": "B1",
"name": "chase around a corner: after losing sight it stays a chase (HUNTING, at pursuit speed) at least until the predicted route is checked or it sees the prey again; it never turns CURIOUS",
"ok": true,
"note": "16 chases lost round a corner (the prey running on): kept the chase in 16; saw the prey again within 3 s in 12; mean speed in the first 1.5 s (lunge recovery excluded) 198 px/s (chase 292); reached the last-seen spot 75% (runs not re-seen); CURIOUS in 0; pursuit sources ear, route, lkp; states HUNTING, SEARCHING"
},
{
"id": "B3",
"name": "recent running out of sight updates the pursuit: followed by ear, the chase kept, its goal nearer the real prey than when the prey goes on quietly; the goal moves far less than the steps' blur (no per-footstep jitter)",
"ok": true,
"note": "14 paired chases (same seed; out of sight the prey runs on, or creeps on quietly): followed by ear in 92%; the pursuit goal was 192 px from a running prey vs 315 px from a quiet one (closer in 78%); CURIOUS 0; largest jump of the ear goal between ticks 24 px, against 425 px between the raw heard steps (the steps' blur)"
},
{
"id": "B2",
"name": "a silent change of route fools it: the predicted route continues the heading it saw, away from where the prey really went",
"ok": true,
"note": "12 chases where the prey, out of sight, crept back the way it came: the Hound planned a predicted route in 7, ahead along the heading it saw in 85%, i.e. farther from the real prey than the spot where it vanished in 85%; the prey stayed unseen for 6 s in 25% (the rest were seen on the way to that spot)"
},
{
"id": "B4",
"name": "no evidence: the blind pursuit becomes a search, confidence decays, and the Hound gives up for a stated reason",
"ok": true,
"note": "10 preys gone without a trace (silently 1200-1800 px away): gave up in 10 (after 13 s on average); sequences HUNTING>SEARCHING>FRUSTRATED>ROAMING; reasons memory faded / nowhere left to look; blind phase ended: predicted route checked"
}
